<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - Cons Modder Q2 pre-capex into loss.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Cons Modder Q2 pre-capex into loss.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-June versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Cash profit before capital spending</p>
<p>				    1.56 loss vs 0.09 profit</p>
<p>    Capital spending	  1.02	vs 1.01</p>
<p>    Tonnes milled	     89,000    vs 93,000</p>
<p>    Gold output (kg)	  367	 vs 386</p>
<p>    Yield (gram/t)	    4.12	vs 4.15</p>
<p>    Cost (rand/kg)	    53,134    vs 51,870</p>
<p>    Revenue (rand/kg)	 49,324    vs 50.777</p>
<p>Full name: Consolidated Modderfontein Mines Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said that during the next quarter the metallurgical, surface transport and workshop sections will be closed down leading to the retrenchment of about 90 employees.</p>
<p>They said capital commitments amount to 59,000 rand.</p>
<p>The firm became a wholly-owned subsidiary of Harmony Gold Mining Co Ltd in June 30, 1997. The June results have been restated to coincide with the Harmony close of costs.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
